<MockPage Path="/practice/wills" Label="Wills and estates" InMenu="false" Parent="/practice">
    <p>A will says who gets what, and who sees to it. We draw up wills for families, farmers and businesses in the
        Swartland, and wind up estates when the time comes.</p>
    <MockSection Path="/practice/wills/covers" Heading="What a will covers">
        <ul>
            <li>Who inherits what: the house, the farm, the savings, a keepsake.</li>
            <li>Your executor, the person who winds up your estate.</li>
            <li>A guardian for children under 18, and a trust to hold what they inherit until they're older.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>You sign every page, and two witnesses of 14 or older sign with you. A witness, or their spouse, shouldn't
            be an heir.</p>
    </MockSection>
    <MockSection Path="/practice/wills/without" Heading="Without a will">
        <p>The Intestate Succession Act decides for you. Your spouse and children share by a set formula, and your
            spouse gets at least R250,000. A partner you never married may get nothing.</p>
    </MockSection>
    <MockSection Path="/practice/wills/after-divorce" Heading="After a divorce">
        <p>A divorce doesn't cancel your will. If you die within three months of it, the will is read as if your former
            spouse had died before you, unless it clearly says otherwise. After those three months, the will counts as
            written, your former spouse included. So change it within the three months.</p>
    </MockSection>
    <MockSection Path="/practice/wills/in-community" Heading="Married in community of property?">
        <p>Half the joint estate is your spouse's own. Your will can only leave your half.</p>
    </MockSection>
    <MockSection Path="/practice/wills/estate" Heading="When someone dies: the estate">
        <ol>
            <li>The death is reported to the Master of the High Court within 14 days.</li>
            <li>The Master appoints the executor, with letters of executorship.</li>
            <li>The executor lists what the estate owns and owes, and calls on creditors in the Gazette.</li>
            <li>The account lies open for 21 days, then the heirs are paid.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Most estates take six to twelve months. The executor's fee is at most 3.5% of the estate, plus VAT.</p>
    </MockSection>
    <MockSection Path="/practice/wills/fees" Heading="Fees">
        <p>A will from R1,800, drawn up in a week. We keep your signed original in our safe at no charge. A first
            consultation is 30 minutes, R650.</p>
    </MockSection>
